/// Unit tests for the root NodeId NamespaceIndex (NSI) allocation rules of
/// InstantiationService::instantiate_object_async / instantiate_variable_async.
///
/// OPC UA Part 5 section 4.1 forbids server-generated nodes from living in NSI 0
/// ("they are not defined by the OPC Foundation but generated by the Server").
/// The SDK resolves the NSI for a newly instantiated subtree as:
///   1. explicit InstantiationOptions::targetNamespaceIndex wins, else
///   2. the parent's NSI, else (parent is NSI 0)
///   3. fall back to NSI 1 (the spec-reserved local-server slot).
/// The resolved NSI applies to the root AND propagates to mandatory children.
///
/// Separately, Part 3 section 5.2.4: a child's BrowseName is copied from the type
/// declaration and does NOT follow the NodeId NSI - a 0:Foo member declaration
/// yields a 0:Foo instance member even when its NodeId lands in NSI 1.

